    {
      "id": "1549944276287361149",
      "type": "Reply",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-17T00:45:12.039+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "We're working on an open source high speed SerDes for the open PDKs not worse than the gf180mcu family; due to sponsoring reasons we're targeting IHP's SG13CMOS5L first with a planned 25GBASE-R performance (likely restricting how far the next redriver can be from the ASIC) and then hoping to port with that same speed but concessions on the PCB side to the somewhat slower sky130A process. \n\nA \"back\" port to gf180mcuD will happen as well, it's order w.r.t. the sky130A one is uncertain.\nOn that process we're not planning to (substantially) exceed 10Gbit/s though, and as long as it works with a commodity 10GBASE-SR SFP+ optic on a decent but non-expensive PCB with good respect paid to not incurring substantial loss or problematic reflections between the signal conditioning chip in the transceiver and the custom ASIC, I'm happy. \nI want fairly lax burden for data export from the custom ASIC even if import is allowed to need a signal conditioning retimer COTS chip within less than 10cm of the custom ASIC.\nAt least the 2.5 Gbit/s of PCIe Gen1 should probably work natively from the ASIC though, even if perhaps under reasonable restrictions to PCB signal loss/connector quality, so long as it'd at least work with normal M.2 NVMe drives. It's still like 800~900 million byte per second through the usual 4-lane connection, so e.g. a camera with an \"either\" M.2 local recording \"or\" SFP+ 10G Ethernet with extra 15$ chip needed for receiving at more than 1Gbit/s (could let the same SFP+ optic do both directions asymmetrically just with two single fiber cables instead of LC-duplex that go to separate switch ports) like if one doesn't feel like configuring the switch to handle the asymmetric link topology.",
      "author": {
        "id": "262706220073222144",
        "name": "namibj",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "namibj",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-09_media/f885abc0dddd0a33e4d4991b3c99091d-7ACD2.png"
